# Cloudflare Pages reads this file automatically and applies these headers
# to matching responses. This is what stops a visitor's browser from ever
# getting stuck showing an old, broken version of the site after a new
# deploy — the exact issue found on 2026-07-22.
#
# The problem: the page shell (index.html) was being cached by browsers
# with no explicit instruction, so some browsers kept serving an old,
# already-fetched copy indefinitely (closing/reopening the browser does
# NOT clear this cache — only a hard refresh or a cache expiry does).
#
# The fix: tell every browser to always re-check the page shell with the
# server before using a cached copy (no-cache forces a fast revalidation,
# not a full re-download every time). The actual JS/CSS/image files Vite
# builds get a unique hash in their filename on every build — so those are
# safe to cache "forever"; a new deploy simply produces new filenames, the
# old cached ones are just never referenced again.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/logo-compact.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/logo-full.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
